---
import Icon from '@/components/icons/icon.astro';
import LegalPage from '@/components/ui/legal-page.astro';
import { site } from '@/config/site';
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/base-layout.astro';

const summary = [
  { icon: 'phone', text: 'What you enter stays on your phone. We have no servers and never receive it.' },
  { icon: 'hidden', text: 'No account, no ads, no analytics, no tracking.' },
  { icon: 'export', text: 'A backup or export leaves your phone only when you send it somewhere.' },
] as const;
---

<BaseLayout title="Privacy policy" description="How Lifio handles your data: everything you enter stays on your phone. No account, no servers, no ads, no tracking.">
  <LegalPage eyebrow="Privacy" title="Privacy policy" lead="Lifio is built so that we never see your data. This page explains exactly what that means.">
    <ul slot="summary" class="grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-3">
      {
        summary.map((item) => (
          <li class="flex flex-col gap-3 rounded-card bg-focal p-5 text-on-focal">
            <Icon name={item.icon} size={24} />
            <p class="leading-relaxed">{item.text}</p>
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ul>

    <h2>Who we are</h2>
    <p>
      Lifio is an app for Android made by <strong>{site.developer}</strong> (“we”). This policy covers the Lifio app and this website. Questions go to{' '}
      <a href={`mailto:${site.supportEmail}`}>{site.supportEmail}</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>What Lifio stores, and where</h2>
    <p>
      Everything you enter in Lifio is stored in the app’s private storage on your phone, which other apps cannot read. That includes your first name, an
      optional profile photo, habits and their ticks, check-ins, mood, health logs (such as sleep, weight, steps, heart rate and symptoms), water, notes, and
      your settings and reminder times.
    </p>
    <p>Lifio has no account and no servers. We never receive, see, sell or share any of it.</p>

    <h2>What can leave your phone</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Backups and exports you make.</strong> When you create a backup or export a spreadsheet, Android asks where to save or send the file. It goes
        only where you choose, and from then on it is looked after by that place (for example your own cloud drive or email).
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Android’s own device backup.</strong> If backup is turned on in your phone’s settings, Android may include Lifio’s data in your phone backup
        to your Google account, as it does for most apps. That backup belongs to you and is managed by Google; we cannot access it.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>App update check.</strong> When Lifio opens, it asks Expo’s update service whether a newer version of the app is available. That request
        carries technical details only (the app version, Android, and the update channel) and, like any internet request, your IP address. It carries none of
        your entries.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Permissions Lifio asks for</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Notifications and exact alarms</strong>, only when you turn on a reminder, so reminders arrive on time. They are scheduled on the phone itself.</li>
      <li>
        <strong>Fingerprint, face or screen lock</strong>, only if you turn on App lock. Android checks it; Lifio only learns whether unlocking succeeded.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Photos and files</strong> through Android’s own pickers, only when you choose a profile photo or a backup to restore. Lifio sees just the item
        you pick. A photo is copied into the app’s private storage.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>Lifio does not use your camera, microphone, location, contacts, or health sensors.</p>

    <h2>No ads, no analytics, no tracking</h2>
    <p>
      Lifio contains no advertising, analytics or tracking code, and never follows you across other apps or websites. Google Play may collect its own
      information when you install or update apps, under Google’s privacy policy.
    </p>

    <h2>Health information</h2>
    <p>
      The health details you log are for your own reference. In version 1.0 Lifio does not connect to Health Connect or any other health service. If a later
      version adds that, it will read only what you allow, keep it on your phone like everything else, and this policy will be updated first.
    </p>

    <h2>Keeping and deleting your data</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Delete any entry inside the app. Deleted notes wait in Recently deleted for 30 days, then are removed for good.</li>
      <li>Clear one area, or everything, in Settings → Data.</li>
      <li>Uninstalling Lifio deletes all of its data from your phone. Keep a backup if you may want it later: we cannot recover anything for you.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>As there is no account, there is no account to delete and nothing held by us.</p>

    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>Lifio is meant for adults and is not directed at children under 13. It collects nothing from anyone, children included.</p>

    <h2>This website</h2>
    <p>
      This website sets no cookies and contains no analytics or tracking. If you pick Light or Dark, your browser remembers that choice on your device;
      it is never sent to us. Its fonts are served from the site itself. Like any website, its hosting provider
      may keep short-lived technical logs, such as IP addresses, to run and protect the service.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>
      If this policy changes, the new version will appear here with a new date. We will never start sending your entries anywhere: a change like that would
      break Lifio’s first promise.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Write to <a href={`mailto:${site.supportEmail}`}>{site.supportEmail}</a> with any question about privacy. A person reads every message.
    </p>
  </LegalPage>
</BaseLayout>
